{"duration_api_ms":305627,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"fb8a9640-e103-4209-bbcc-56fb32603975","total_cost_usd":0.8723925999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42360,"cache_read_input_tokens":2388993,"output_tokens":22083,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":9287},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42360,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2430,"cache_read_input_tokens":58061,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1323},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4031,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004116,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":104,"outputTokens":22083,"cacheReadInputTokens":2388993,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42360,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8682765999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":9287,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":53,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"blocked\",\"summary\":\"The LVM volume was fully built, mounted at /srv/data, and grown to 2.1GB with verified data integrity intact across the grow. However the mandatory reboot step left node1 unresponsive to exec for ~48 minutes afterward, most likely because the /etc/fstab entry for /srv/data lacked \\\"nofail\\\" and depends on a custom systemd unit — a failure there very likely pushed the boot into an emergency shell requiring console/root-password input, which the exec-only tool cannot provide. I cannot verify post-restart recovery for node1.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1: entire 20GB vda disk was already partitioned for bios_grub/boot/root with no free space and no spare block device for a real LVM PV.\",\"Created two 1200MiB backing files under /var/lib/lvm-loop and attached them as loop devices (/dev/loop0, /dev/loop1) to serve as PVs.\",\"pvcreate on loop0, vgcreate datavg, lvcreate -L 1000M datalv, mkfs.xfs, mounted the LV at /srv/data.\",\"Wrote a text file and a 50MB random blob to /srv/data and recorded sha256 checksums as a baseline.\",\"pvcreate on loop1, vgextend datavg with loop1, lvextend datalv to <2.15GiB, and xfs_growfs /srv/data while it stayed mounted (online grow) — df confirmed 2.1G filesystem size, satisfying the >=2GB requirement.\",\"Verified both files' sha256 checksums matched the originals after the grow, proving data integrity was preserved.\",\"Created /usr/local/sbin/attach-lvm-loops.sh plus a systemd oneshot unit loop-lvm-setup.service (DefaultDependencies=no, Before=local-fs-pre.target, WantedBy=local-fs-pre.target) to reattach the loop devices at boot (matched by backing-file path via LVM's loop_file device-ID, so it's robust to loop-number reassignment) and run vgchange -ay datavg; enabled the service.\",\"Added an /etc/fstab entry for /dev/datavg/datalv at /srv/data with x-systemd.requires=loop-lvm-setup.service, but without nofail.\",\"Validated the fstab/systemd wiring live before rebooting: unmounted /srv/data, deactivated datavg, detached both loop devices, then started the generated srv-data.mount unit directly — it correctly ran the loop-attach service first, reattached the loops, reactivated the VG, and remounted /srv/data at 2.1G with both files' checksums verified intact.\",\"Captured a pre-reboot baseline: boot_id, systemctl is-enabled loop-lvm-setup.service (enabled), df -h /srv/data, lvs sizing, and file checksums.\",\"Issued a native reboot (backgrounded 'sleep 2 && systemctl reboot' so the exec acknowledgement returned before disconnection) — connection reset confirmed the node went down.\",\"Polled node1 with a stable boot-id check repeatedly over roughly 48 minutes; every attempt returned a connection-level error (reset/timeout), never a boot_id value, indicating the node has not returned to a state where exec is served.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"LV mounted at /srv/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-465c11713ead47d7\"],\"summary\":\"mkfs.xfs + mount succeeded; df -h showed /dev/mapper/datavg-datalv mounted at /srv/data.\"},{\"requirement\":\"LV grown to >=2GB while mounted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-63468be3b56c49c2\"],\"summary\":\"vgextend + lvextend -L 2200M + xfs_growfs run against the still-mounted /srv/data; df -h confirmed 2.1G filesystem size and lvextend log shows resize from 1000MiB to <2.15GiB without unmounting.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Contents stay intact through the grow\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-18d1962c74a94b6c\",\"cmd-be2a76fb4295431f\"],\"summary\":\"sha256 checksums of a text file and a 50MB random blob recorded before the grow and re-verified (OK) immediately after xfs_growfs completed.\"},{\"requirement\":\"No spare disk existed; justification for loop-device-backed PVs\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-346aebfbbcd44848\",\"cmd-034819ab045b4fbc\"],\"summary\":\"lsblk and parted free-space check showed the single 20GB disk fully partitioned with zero free space, ruling out adding a real second partition/disk as a PV.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Boot-time persistence design and pre-reboot validation\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1e16605c231341b3\",\"cmd-828b0ccc1e0e4dc7\",\"cmd-90ba4caacd1048d9\"],\"summary\":\"systemd unit enabled, fstab entry added, and the generated srv-data.mount unit started directly (after manually detaching loops/VG) to prove the dependency chain reattaches loops, activates the VG, and remounts /srv/data with data intact — without requiring a real reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline (mandatory protocol)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1676285ff0d54a29\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id, service enablement, df -h, lvs sizing, and file checksums immediately before issuing the reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection (mandatory protocol)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-18798cc7e73d481c\",\"cmd-49c8a36fe2584b22\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded reboot command returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately; the very next exec call failed with connection reset, confirming the node went down shortly after acknowledgement.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity and post-restart recovery proof (mandatory protocol) — NOT MET for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-de5771ca73b649ab\",\"cmd-74bcb4a571914e30\",\"cmd-b1722f8532ad4551\",\"cmd-c1655ef8f085447d\",\"cmd-6d054b78293e4a9c\",\"cmd-d611597432df430c\"],\"summary\":\"Repeated boot_id polls across ~48 minutes post-reboot all failed at the connection level (reset/timeout), never returning a boot_id. This is evidence of the limitation, not of recovery: node1's restart persistence and post-restart health cannot be confirmed, most likely because the /srv/data fstab entry (added without nofail) triggered an emergency-mode boot that requires console access unavailable through the exec tool.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"blocked","summary":"The LVM volume was fully built, mounted at /srv/data, and grown to 2.1GB with verified data integrity intact across the grow. However the mandatory reboot step left node1 unresponsive to exec for ~48 minutes afterward, most likely because the /etc/fstab entry for /srv/data lacked \"nofail\" and depends on a custom systemd unit — a failure there very likely pushed the boot into an emergency shell requiring console/root-password input, which the exec-only tool cannot provide. I cannot verify post-restart recovery for node1.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1: entire 20GB vda disk was already partitioned for bios_grub/boot/root with no free space and no spare block device for a real LVM PV.","Created two 1200MiB backing files under /var/lib/lvm-loop and attached them as loop devices (/dev/loop0, /dev/loop1) to serve as PVs.","pvcreate on loop0, vgcreate datavg, lvcreate -L 1000M datalv, mkfs.xfs, mounted the LV at /srv/data.","Wrote a text file and a 50MB random blob to /srv/data and recorded sha256 checksums as a baseline.","pvcreate on loop1, vgextend datavg with loop1, lvextend datalv to <2.15GiB, and xfs_growfs /srv/data while it stayed mounted (online grow) — df confirmed 2.1G filesystem size, satisfying the >=2GB requirement.","Verified both files' sha256 checksums matched the originals after the grow, proving data integrity was preserved.","Created /usr/local/sbin/attach-lvm-loops.sh plus a systemd oneshot unit loop-lvm-setup.service (DefaultDependencies=no, Before=local-fs-pre.target, WantedBy=local-fs-pre.target) to reattach the loop devices at boot (matched by backing-file path via LVM's loop_file device-ID, so it's robust to loop-number reassignment) and run vgchange -ay datavg; enabled the service.","Added an /etc/fstab entry for /dev/datavg/datalv at /srv/data with x-systemd.requires=loop-lvm-setup.service, but without nofail.","Validated the fstab/systemd wiring live before rebooting: unmounted /srv/data, deactivated datavg, detached both loop devices, then started the generated srv-data.mount unit directly — it correctly ran the loop-attach service first, reattached the loops, reactivated the VG, and remounted /srv/data at 2.1G with both files' checksums verified intact.","Captured a pre-reboot baseline: boot_id, systemctl is-enabled loop-lvm-setup.service (enabled), df -h /srv/data, lvs sizing, and file checksums.","Issued a native reboot (backgrounded 'sleep 2 && systemctl reboot' so the exec acknowledgement returned before disconnection) — connection reset confirmed the node went down.","Polled node1 with a stable boot-id check repeatedly over roughly 48 minutes; every attempt returned a connection-level error (reset/timeout), never a boot_id value, indicating the node has not returned to a state where exec is served."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"LV mounted at /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-465c11713ead47d7"],"summary":"mkfs.xfs + mount succeeded; df -h showed /dev/mapper/datavg-datalv mounted at /srv/data."},{"requirement":"LV grown to >=2GB while mounted","command_ids":["cmd-63468be3b56c49c2"],"summary":"vgextend + lvextend -L 2200M + xfs_growfs run against the still-mounted /srv/data; df -h confirmed 2.1G filesystem size and lvextend log shows resize from 1000MiB to <2.15GiB without unmounting."},{"requirement":"Contents stay intact through the grow","command_ids":["cmd-18d1962c74a94b6c","cmd-be2a76fb4295431f"],"summary":"sha256 checksums of a text file and a 50MB random blob recorded before the grow and re-verified (OK) immediately after xfs_growfs completed."},{"requirement":"No spare disk existed; justification for loop-device-backed PVs","command_ids":["cmd-346aebfbbcd44848","cmd-034819ab045b4fbc"],"summary":"lsblk and parted free-space check showed the single 20GB disk fully partitioned with zero free space, ruling out adding a real second partition/disk as a PV."},{"requirement":"Boot-time persistence design and pre-reboot validation","command_ids":["cmd-1e16605c231341b3","cmd-828b0ccc1e0e4dc7","cmd-90ba4caacd1048d9"],"summary":"systemd unit enabled, fstab entry added, and the generated srv-data.mount unit started directly (after manually detaching loops/VG) to prove the dependency chain reattaches loops, activates the VG, and remounts /srv/data with data intact — without requiring a real reboot."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline (mandatory protocol)","command_ids":["cmd-1676285ff0d54a29"],"summary":"Captured boot_id, service enablement, df -h, lvs sizing, and file checksums immediately before issuing the reboot."},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection (mandatory protocol)","command_ids":["cmd-18798cc7e73d481c","cmd-49c8a36fe2584b22"],"summary":"Backgrounded reboot command returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately; the very next exec call failed with connection reset, confirming the node went down shortly after acknowledgement."},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity and post-restart recovery proof (mandatory protocol) — NOT MET for node1","command_ids":["cmd-de5771ca73b649ab","cmd-74bcb4a571914e30","cmd-b1722f8532ad4551","cmd-c1655ef8f085447d","cmd-6d054b78293e4a9c","cmd-d611597432df430c"],"summary":"Repeated boot_id polls across ~48 minutes post-reboot all failed at the connection level (reset/timeout), never returning a boot_id. This is evidence of the limitation, not of recovery: node1's restart persistence and post-restart health cannot be confirmed, most likely because the /srv/data fstab entry (added without nofail) triggered an emergency-mode boot that requires console access unavailable through the exec tool."}]},"ttft_ms":2285,"type":"result","duration_ms":311220,"uuid":"1e8d76ce-4f6b-4957-a428-ce7022a3df71","ttft_stream_ms":1540,"time_to_request_ms":48,"first_content_frame_ms":2283,"queued_turn_count":0}
